{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"@'\nimport subprocess, tomllib\nrev='8ddf8387b1fb7ce4aee486c8b361dcad0db8e332'\ndef read(p): return subprocess.check_output(['git','show',f'{rev}:{p}']).decode('utf-8')\nd=tomllib.loads(read('docs/requirements/stakeholder-needs.toml'))\nfor key in ('SN-027','SN-008','SN-025'):\n print(key, d.get('need',d.get('requirement',{})).get(key))\nprint('RUBRIC_BLOB', subprocess.check_output(['git','rev-parse',f'{rev}:docs/rubrics/plan-decomposition.md']).decode().strip())\n'@ | python -B -\"","aggregated_output":"SN-027 {'status': 'Approved', 'stakeholder_refs': ['STK-02'], 'tags': ['perf', 'unattended', 'scripts'], 'need': 'A team gets more than one piece of ready work moving at once: ready work **fans out across bounded parallel lanes**, while mutation of the integration branch stays **serialized and gated**.', 'why': 'Concurrency is admitted here on structural grounds, not throughput ones: the WI DAG already encodes what may proceed, so a frontier bounded to one lane idles ready work for no reason; and parallel *integration* is precisely how a reviewed process ships an unreviewed tree � so fan-out is admitted only because it narrows back to a single serialized, gated seam before anything lands. No instrument here measures speedup, so a quantified-speedup justification would be unfalsifiable as written; the observability such a claim would need is carried instead by the lane-utilisation report.', 'priority': 'S', 'acceptance': 'A launch with independent ready WIs runs up to the configured worker ceiling (default 2) concurrently in isolated worktrees; every finished branch lands through one serial, fail-closed integrator that runs the declared bar on the composed tree; `--jobs 1` preserves the serial semantic; a declared pause stops claiming and drains what is already in flight; a crash at any lifecycle boundary recovers from Git history alone, without double-assignment or half-integrated authoritative state. Spec of record: `docs/archive/specs/parallel-wi-dispatch.2026-07-20.md` + `docs/concurrency-restructure.md`.'}\r\nSN-008 {'status': 'Approved', 'stakeholder_refs': ['STK-03'], 'need': 'A reader can believe a **pass verdict**: gates are **honest**, and a pass verdict never hides a skipped check, a stub, or an unmet declared criterion.', 'why': \"*Trust what ships*; a false pass is worse than a failure. The verdict is named as a verdict � the word PASS � never by hue: a colour word as the only name for the system's most important signal does not exist for a substantial class of readers, and the kit's console output carries zero ANSI colour in any case.\", 'priority': 'M', 'acceptance': 'The harness **fails** (not skips) on a missing required tool � the explicitly-requested `--lenient` local mode is the one sanctioned degrade to SKIP (SR-006), never a CI/gate default; the no-stub detector and the privacy/secrets floor run at their declared gate.'}\r\nSN-025 {'status': 'Approved', 'stakeholder_refs': ['STK-01'], 'tags': ['unattended', 'loop'], 'need': \"**With no human curating what comes next**, a configured LLM agent implements toward the vision � fully autonomously where enabled � deriving its own next work from the repository's tracked state. (The launcher that starts it is SN-034's obligation; this need is the self-direction.)\", 'why': 'Walk-away autonomy is the whole promise of the unattended layer: if a human must hand-maintain a next-step pointer, the loop is attended in practice and the pointer rots against the registry it paraphrases. Extends SN-006 (a *resumable* unattended run) into a *self-directing* one.', 'priority': 'S', 'acceptance': 'A plain launch derives what to do next from the tracked WI DAG plus Git � never from prose or a hand-maintained pointer, and never from predefined tracks; the ready frontier is ordered deterministically, so two readers of the same registry dispatch the same work; the status surface a human reads is generated from that tracked state, never hand-copied.'}\r\nRUBRIC_BLOB 89674a5a12463d7878348dde9d2849da4f711b63\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
