{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command 'git show 8ddf8387b1fb7ce4aee486c8b361dcad0db8e332:docs/requirements/interfaces.toml | Select-Object -Skip 492 -First 15; git show 8ddf8387b1fb7ce4aee486c8b361dcad0db8e332:docs/requirements/interfaces.toml | Select-Object -Skip 1113 -First 15; Get-Content project-trajectory/PROCESS.md | Select-Object -Skip 956 -First 38; git show 8ddf8387b1fb7ce4aee486c8b361dcad0db8e332:docs/plans/WI-996/plan.md | Select-Object -Skip 132 -First 9'","aggregated_output":"[interface.IF-022]\r\nowner = \"docs/stack.ini\"\r\nconsumers = [\"scripts/check\", \"external:downstream adopter\"]\r\nchannel = \"file\"\r\ndata = \"sections: paths, product, tiers, coverage, arch-map, readability, bars, step:NAME\"\r\nversion = \"v1\"\r\nstatus = \"Drafted\"\r\ninterface_to_external = \"B-05\"\r\ncoincident = \"\"\"The format is what the adopter writes and every reader parses; a copy that reads as this format declares is the whole of what the seam delivers, and what the rows say is judged at their own tiers.\"\"\"\r\nnotes = \"\"\"Published contract, not a single consumer: 9 kit scripts read docs/stack.ini directly (check, agent_common, dispatch, check_doc_refs, check_trajectory, integrate, run_menu, trunk_step, plus this row), and every downstream adopter authors their own copy - naming one reader would misstate the file's role. Ties to B-05 as the template's own delivered declared-policy format.\"\"\"\r\n\r\n[interface.IF-023]\r\nowner = \"docs/work/\"\r\nconsumers = [\"scripts/check_trajectory\", \"external:downstream adopter\"]\r\nchannel = \"file\"\r\n[interface.IF-080]\r\nowner = \"scripts/integrate\"\r\nconsumers = [\"external:downstream adopter\"]\r\nchannel = \"exit-code\"\r\ndata = \"claim | refresh | attest | integrate | done-when-hold | audit; nonzero exit on any refusal, with the reason named\"\r\nversion = \"v1\"\r\nstatus = \"Drafted\"\r\ncomponent = \"CMP-008\"\r\ninterface_to_external = \"B-05\"\r\nbridged_by = [\"DA-013\"]\r\n\r\n[interface.IF-154]\r\nowner = \"scripts/integrate\"\r\nrequestors = [\"scripts/lane\", \"external:downstream adopter\"]\r\nchannel = \"cli\"\r\nempty* perfectly truthfully.\r\n\r\nReviews use this block — in `log.md`, or as a `docs/reviews/WI-<n>-<PHASE>.md`\r\nverdict file under the review layer (work-item-scoped names; serial counters\r\nrace under concurrency):\r\n\r\n```\r\n### <HAT or REVIEWER> — <Gate> — Round <r> — <YYYY-MM-DD>\r\nVERDICT: APPROVE|CHANGES-REQUESTED findings=<N>\r\nFindings:\r\n- [BLOCKER|MAJOR|MINOR] <ID or area> → <issue> → <suggested change> → @<owner>\r\n```\r\n\r\nSitting sign-offs live in the **Sittings** table in `log.md`; the driver\r\nrecords the gate decision there, cites it from status.md's *Stage* line,\r\nand requests acceptance per the declared gate authority (§4).\r\n\r\n**Voice policy — warmth has a layer boundary.** Personality is a human value, not\r\na machine one: **human-facing** output (CLI narration, a kickoff greeting, a\r\nrelease-checklist intro) may carry warmth and **dry wit at most**;\r\n**machine/agent-facing** output — this protocol's findings and verdicts,\r\nsubagent prompts, registry cells, commit messages — stays **literal, terse,\r\nstructured: no whimsy**. Levity there costs tokens, reads ambiguously to the\r\nnext agent (irony/understatement is exactly what a parser misreads), and\r\nerodes the honesty/severity signal this protocol depends on. Default voice is\r\n**restrained**\r\n(\"direct and concrete; dry wit at most; never at the expense of clarity or\r\nhonesty\"); a project may expose an optional, named **tone knob** to dial levity\r\nup or down — never a baked-in persona, since no single tone fits both a\r\nmedical-device repo and a game studio.\r\n\r\n### Change intake — routing a problem to the spine\r\n\r\nAn inbound problem routes by **which registry row it contradicts** — that\r\nclassification, not the fix, is step 1. Then check the parent obligation and\r\nselected design before treating the violation as a coverage gap:\r\n\r\n```mermaid\r\n\r\n| Plan-WI | Title | Covers | Interfaces | Predecessors |\r\n|---|---|---|---|---|\r\n| P1 | The spine set on reserved ids: LLR-a, TC-a to TC-f, the SR-156, LLR-207 and TC-132 amendments, the arms map, the bound stated | D30; D31; D32; D33; D34; D35; D36; D37; D38; D39; D40; D41; D42; SR-156; TC-132 | IF-022; IF-080; IF-154 | |\r\n| P2 | The tests alone, tagged, under strict marks, and the fixtures' key; no shipped file | D7; D8; D9; D10; D11; D12; D13; D14; D15; D16; D17; D31; D32; D33; D34; D35; SR-156 | IF-022; IF-080; IF-154; IF-173 | P1 |\r\n| P3 | The shared primitives: read_blobs, normal_test_paths, last_review_record, declared_roots | D8; D14; SR-156; TC-205 | no interface: kitlib primitives called inside CMP-008, and review_set's IF-309 surface is unchanged | P2 |\r\n| P4 | kitlib/red_mark.py: read_bars, the count, the table, both refusals; its manifest row | D3; D7; D8; D9; D10; D11; D13; D14; D15; D16; SR-156 | no interface: intra-module to CMP-008, called only by integrate | P3 |\r\n| P5 | attest: one parse, the check in preflight, IF-080's body, exact size stamp | D7; D8; D15; SR-156; TC-132; TC-417 | IF-080; IF-154; IF-173 | P4 |\r\n| P6 | refresh: the landing arm after staging, IF-080's body | D7; D16; SR-156; TC-132 | IF-080; IF-173 | P4 |\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
